all experiments are trained under the same setting with HGNetV2-B0 by 4-fold cross:
1) imagenet GAP head : lb 0.860 (an earlier experiment with different fold and lr gives 0.863)
2) LSE head: lb0.876 (EMA gives 0.874)
3) time gated SED: lb 0.851 (EMA gives 0.855)

LSE is a method for MIL (multiple instead learning. you can google for more)
in terms of local CV, time gated SED is the best (much better), followed by LSE, GAP.

my LSE head:

def lse_pool(x, dim=1, r=10.0):
    T = x.size(dim)
    return torch.logsumexp(r * x, dim=dim) / r - math.log(T) / r

def forward(self, ...):
        ...
        last = self.backbone(spec) #torch.Size([32, 2048, 8, 8])
        last = last.mean(dim=2)      # (B, 2048, T)
        last = last.transpose(1, 2)   # (B, T, 2048) 
        time_logit = self.head(last)         # (B, T, 234)
        logit = lse_pool(time_logit, dim=1)  # (B, 234) to BCE loss

